{"id":"northern_rockies_montane","display_name":"Northern Rockies Montane","enabled":true,"description":"Calibrated from The Reserve at Moonlight Basin in Big Sky, Montana. A high-elevation Northern Rockies conifer-dominant visual palette with minor deciduous/aspen-like accents and occasional dead-tree snags.","reference_courses":["Moonlight Basin.course"],"reference_context":{"course_name":"Reserve @ Moonlight Basin","author_name":"HouseofMogh420 TTV","course_theme_id":12,"par":72,"holes":18,"real_world_region":"Big Sky / Madison Range / Northern Rocky Mountains, Montana"},"all_speedtree_tree_count":9050,"natural_reference_tree_count":7219,"excluded_vertical_massing_count":1831,"profile_tree_count":7219,"coverage_of_natural_reference_population":1,"profile_prefab_count":19,"terrain_alignment_tolerance_m":0.75,"scale_defaults":{"x":{"p10":0.836833,"p50":0.999315,"p90":1.170644},"y":{"p10":0.836833,"p50":0.999315,"p90":1.170644},"z":{"p10":0.836833,"p50":0.999315,"p90":1.170644}},"calibration_notes":["Vertically buried/raised scenery-massing trees are excluded using the Beta 5 terrain-alignment filter.","All 19 natural-placement prefabs are retained because the palette is already highly concentrated; the three Norway Spruce prefabs account for about 95.8% of natural tree placements.","The real Big Sky/Northern Rockies montane forest is dominated by spruce/fir/pine/Douglas-fir associations with lodgepole pine and aspen. The course's Norway Spruce, Scots Pine and generic conifers are retained as visual analogs where exact game species do not match local taxonomy.","White Oak and River Birch prefabs form only a small minority of the profile and are retained as deciduous/aspen-like visual accents rather than literal local species claims.","Rare dead-tree prefabs are preserved at their observed low weights because standing snags/dead conifer forms are visually appropriate in a mountain forest."],"assets":[{"path":"Assets/Foliage/SpeedTree8/Trees/Spruce_Norway/Prefabs/Spru